---
alwaysApply: true
---
- These rules apply only to work on the v2 version of the code and API.
- The file v2-schema.dat (DBML format) is a reference for what the sqlite v2 database should be
- The development plan is in the file v2-api-implementation-editable.plan.md
- If you come across the word "STOP" in the plan, stop work and wait for user feedback
- All v2 database columns use snake_case
- All API fields use camelCase. API camelCase fields correspond directly to database snake_case fields.  Example:  orgUid -> org_uid, metaKey -> meta_key
- When testing, stop/kill processes when finished
- CHIA_ROOT directory is ~/.chia/mainnet/ and directory for cadt config and database for v2 will be ~/.chia/mainnet/cadt/v2/

# Primary Keys
- Data tables: UUID v4 (varchar(36))
- System tables: INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT

# Foreign Keys
- Application-level validation (no DB constraints)
- Check both main table AND staging table for references
- Enables staging multiple related records before commit

# Timestamps
- Automatically managed by Sequelize (`created_at`, `updated_at`)
- Rejected if provided in POST/PUT requests

# API Request Patterns (CRITICAL - Follows V1)
- Update Requests: MUST include ALL fields, not just the ones being updated
- Create Requests: Include all required fields
- Validation: Same validation schema used for both CREATE and UPDATE operations

# Testing
- Always run v2 tests individually to avoid v1 test interference
- Work iteratively and write and run tests when any API endpoint is created or modified
